      ⎕RL←16807
      ⎕RL
16807

      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ random numbers differ between interpreters
      ?5
2

      ⎕RL
34697829103953066

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #31, 2026-08-11):
      ⍝ ⎕RL is documented as non-negative (apl2lrm.txt p.322); GNU APL's
      ⍝ internal 64-bit LCG state used to be exposed to ⎕RL completely
      ⍝ unmasked (raw, could be negative and far outside any documented
      ⍝ domain) -- now masked to its low 63 bits (positive values only,
      ⍝ scaled up to GNU APL's native 64-bit integers, not clamped down
      ⍝ to APL2's original 32-bit ¯2+2*31 upper bound -- user's explicit
      ⍝ design call). Negative assignments are rejected immediately;
      ⍝ 0 is accepted (confirmed via the Hull-Dobell full-period
      ⍝ theorem that this specific LCG -- a≡1 mod 4, c odd, m=2^64 --
      ⍝ has no fixed point, so no seed, including 0, can ever produce a
      ⍝ degenerate/constant sequence).
      ⍝
      ⎕RL←¯1
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕RL←¯1
      ^  ^
      )MORE
⎕RL must be a non-negative integer; GNU APL's valid range is 0 to 9223372036854775807 (2*63-1) -- wider than APL2's documented ¯2+2*31, scaled up to GNU APL's native 64-bit integers (see LanguageVariances.md #31)

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ⎕RL←0
      ⎕RL
0

